## Independently established physical 0215 native geometry

Author inventories for 79/80 match the blind pixel observations.
Both frames have exactly 18 rows and 18 columns of native squares,
19 native grid lines each way, two small cells per unit.
Do not count the external inspection overlay as graph geometry.

fig-79:
- One left panel; x/y positive arrows; x labels -2,-1,O,1,2,3;
  y labels -2,-1,1,2. The source origin glyph reads italic O.
- Native origin is seven cells from left, nine from top. The frame
  corresponds to x=-3.5..5.5, y=-4.5..4.5.
- Five horizontal pieces (n,n) to (n+1,n), n=-2,-1,0,1,2.
- Hollow right ends (-1,-2),(0,-1),(1,0),(2,1),(3,2).
- Left starts have no hollow markers. Their included-left interpretation
  comes from [n,n+1[ prose; a new separate filled-dot object is not claimed.
- The y=0 piece overlaps the x axis; there are no vertical graph jumps,
  extra panels, labelled arbitrary points or dashed curves.

fig-80:
- One right panel; x/y positive arrows; x labels -3,-2,-1,O,1,2,3;
  y labels 1,2,3. The source origin glyph reads italic O.
- Native origin nine cells from left, eleven from top. Frame corresponds
  to x=-4.5..4.5, y=-3.5..5.5.
- Six ascending straight pieces (n,0) to (n+1,1), n=-3,-2,-1,0,1,2.
- All six upper-right ends are hollow; lower-left starts meet y=0
  without hollow circles or a separately claimed filled-dot object.
- No drawn vertical reset connections or extra numerical point labels.
  No extension beyond these source pieces is authorized by this inventory.

Supplemental fig-78 crop:
Two rightward number lines, each with labels -3,-2,-1,0,1.
Left x is at the -2 tick; [x]=x. Right [x] is at -1, [x]+1 is at 0,
and x's clear downward pointer is strictly between them.
No exact numerical fractional value is supplied for the right x.
No rectangular grid or additional coordinate-axis name. R1 above is the
only disagreement with the author's geometric inventory.

